{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide SNMPv2c access from node2 to node1 using the community branch-readonly.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"Successful SNMPv2c queries from node2 to node1 directly demonstrate access, and the source ACL is limited to node2. However, the community is represented only as $SNMP_COMMUNITY and redacted in final configuration, so the captured evidence does not prove its literal value was branch-readonly.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1b7cfba5a884c22","cmd-ed5f391b146e47c6","cmd-fc99b47d327549f2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Expose system identity and uptime, with sysLocation set to West Branch and sysContact set to ops@branch.test.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct queries returned sysDescr, sysUpTime, the required contact, and the required location both before and after node1's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1b7cfba5a884c22","cmd-c015518f50774bff","cmd-fc99b47d327549f2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Permit reads through the community but reject writes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Authorized reads succeeded. SET attempts returned noAccess, and follow-up reads confirmed the target values remained unchanged; this behavior persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-07520d5647224fbc","cmd-c015518f50774bff","cmd-fc99b47d327549f2"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the asset register in /srv/legacy2/snmp-readonly-monitoring.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node1 asset register retained its prepared SHA-256 hash and original content through configuration and restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-c474a6b78b454c71","cmd-2bd58a91f36d4e36","cmd-ed5f391b146e47c6"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained Ubuntu 7.10 with kernel 2.6.22-14-generic. Release-native Net-SNMP 5.3.1 packages were installed with zero upgrades, and the installed daemon and client worked after both reboots.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c474a6b78b454c71","cmd-359b085b2b8641ce","cmd-3eb867ade54e43bb","cmd-897dd2f0cab948f0","cmd-ed5f391b146e47c6","cmd-fc99b47d327549f2","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.88,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"Most mutations were necessary: refreshing package metadata, installing legacy-compatible SNMP packages, configuring the daemon, and performing the mandated restarts. One avoidable mutation occurred in cmd-a17cc70b4bbe474c: it wrote a literal $NODE_IP endpoint and temporarily left snmpd stopped; cmd-bad8e6227e364ed8 corrected it. That command also created two pre-branch-monitoring backup files; one supported the correction, but neither was subsequently removed, leaving apparent backup residue. No other unnecessary mutation is evident; final temporary-file inventories were empty and dpkg health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a17cc70b4bbe474c","cmd-bad8e6227e364ed8","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The requested SNMP monitoring behavior is operational: node2 reads node1's identity, uptime, contact, and location; writes are rejected; the node1 asset register is preserved; and the legacy OS and kernel remain intact. Both nodes have strong restart evidence with acknowledged reboots, changed boot identities, and recovered end-to-end monitoring. The sole material evidentiary gap is that the captured output redacts the configured community, so its exact branch-readonly spelling cannot be confirmed.","limitations":["The literal value of $SNMP_COMMUNITY was never captured; successful access proves a configured community works but not that it is exactly branch-readonly.","The fixed after-executor listening-socket snapshots are empty despite direct netstat output and successful remote SNMP queries, creating a minor collector-level inconsistency.","Node2's restart evidence proves boot change, client-package recovery, and end-to-end SNMP recovery, but does not re-check node2's local asset-register data as part of the provider-wide restart protocol.","Systemd service-state collection was unsupported on this legacy release; service recovery was instead demonstrated with init scripts, process/listener checks, and remote queries."]}
